# Repo-scale default: store LF, check out LF, so a Windows shell and a Linux
# runner or mount cannot disagree about a file nobody edited. Added 29 August
# 2026; see the specific rules below, which override this line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The CI build script is executed by `sh` on the Linux runner. Keep shell
# scripts LF regardless of the platform's core.autocrlf, so a CRLF checkout
# cannot break the deploy. (Brief 07 §1 documents the CRLF/LF hazard here.)
# Stated explicitly, after the blanket rule, so weakening the line above
# cannot silently remove the deploy's protection.
*.sh text eol=lf

# 16 tracked binaries. text=auto detects them, but say it, because a corrupted
# font or PDF is a silent failure.
*.pdf   -text
*.woff2 -text
